. * ============================
. * Analysis
. * ============================
. 
. use "$DATA/h4_dataset.dta", clear

. 
. 
. * HYPOTHESIS TEST FOR H4: H4.   Having daughters leads to a larger increase i
> n the support of gender equality for men than for women (with gender equality
>  measured by attitudes) *
. 
.         * Model: Extended linear regression (eregress) - Basic linear regress
> ion with endogenous covariates
.         * Dependent variable = support for gender equality (factorial score o
> f plj0621 plj0622)
.         * Independent variable: number of years with daughter(s)
.         * Control variables: male, age, education, life satisfaction, survey 
> year
. 
.         version 17 // for reproducibility

.         set seed 1984 // for reproducibility

.         sort pid // for reproducibility

.         set processors 2 // for reproducibility
    The maximum number of processors or cores being used is 2.  It can be set
    to any number between 1 and 4.

.         
.         *model
.         eregress gendereq c.ydaughters#i.male i.male age educ lifesat i.syear
> , ///
>                         endogenous(ydaughters = i.male age educ lifesat i.sye
> ar, nore) vce(robust)

Iteration 0:  Log pseudolikelihood = -32280.916  (not concave)
Iteration 1:  Log pseudolikelihood = -32280.916  (backed up)
Iteration 2:  Log pseudolikelihood = -32280.916  

